    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d216-a4">

                <pb facs="0401" n="301" xml:id="pg301"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 to No. 602.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Langston to President Salomon.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince, Hayti</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-12-14"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 14,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. President</hi>: The undersigned has the honor, in
                    acknowledging the receipt of your dispatch of the 9th instant, to state that the
                    subject-matter thereof was yesterday duly brought to the attention of the
                    gentlemen representatives mentioned therein; and the undersigned, as directed by
                    them, has the pleasure to assure your excellency that so soon as the several
                    representatives referred to have communicated with their respective Governments
                    with regard to your proposal to adjudicate and settle the claims for losses of
                    their citizens, as the same are connected with the occurrences on the 22d and
                    23d of September last in this city, they will, each for himself, make reply to
                    your Government according to their pleasure or instructions.</p>
                <p>The undersigned, Mr. President, begs to renew to you the assurance of his sincere
                    distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN MERCER LANGSTON.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
